# Admin / Core Isolation

The Admin Dashboard is an **optional management client**. It is not part of the Piso WiFi operational chain.

## Core (must run without Admin)

Coin, Session, Sales, Router Adapter / MikroTik Driver, PortalServer, SetupServer, StorageManager, InstallationStateManager, W5500, watchdog / loopTask.

## Admin (client only)

Admin talks to Core through existing REST + SSE (`/api/health`, `/api/status`, `/api/events`, existing job APIs).

## Admin synchronization meaning

Synchronizes the Admin UI with authoritative **Renz-Fi Core** state.

It does **not** transfer MikroTik credentials to the browser and does **not** open a new RouterOS login on every Admin connection.

- Fresh router cache → `GET /api/status` only
- Stale cache + credentials present → existing `POST /api/router/cache/sync` worker job (202), never RouterOS on `async_tcp`
- RouterOS unavailable → Dashboard still loads with degraded/unavailable router status

## Never

- Coin / session / sale / internet grant depending on Admin being open
- Live RouterOS login or command sequences on every Admin connect
- Periodic Admin polling of MikroTik (use cached `/api/status` + SSE)
- New `/api/admin/sync` that opens RouterOS
- SD / `writeJson` / RouterOS on `async_tcp`
- Copying MikroTik passwords into browser storage
- Claiming "credentials synchronized" unless a real credential/provisioning operation occurred
- Redesigning Setup Wizard, Captive Portal, or Core managers for Admin UX

## Connect flow

`CONNECT` → existing auth → Core state sync (`GET /api/status`, optional stale worker refresh) → existing Dashboard.

## Sales

ESP32 persists first, then may emit `sales.changed` / `sale.created`. Admin applies a targeted UI patch from `sale.created`. If no SSE client is connected, EventBus must no-op. Core continues.
